§§ `The names and opinions of the cases`

`the registered name of another charity, entered in the general section` MEANS `Name entered in the register` OF "Sunshine Trust", `the registered name`, `entered in the general section`, FALSE
`an alternative registered name of another charity, entered in the general section` MEANS `Name entered in the register` OF "Sunshine Trust", `an alternative registered name`, `entered in the general section`, FALSE
`a previous registered name of another charity, entered in the general section` MEANS `Name entered in the register` OF "Sunshine Trust", `a previous registered name`, `entered in the general section`, FALSE
`the registered name of another charity, entered in the restricted section` MEANS `Name entered in the register` OF "Sunshine Trust", `the registered name`, `entered in the restricted section`, FALSE
`the registered name of a charity that has been deregistered` MEANS `Name entered in the register` OF "Sunshine Trust", `the registered name`, `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`, FALSE
`the registered name of the charity itself` MEANS `Name entered in the register` OF "Hope Foundation Limited", `the registered name`, `entered in the general section`, TRUE

GIVEN entries IS A LIST OF `Name entered in the register`
GIVETH AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name`
`the opinion that only the entries are the same or too similar` entries MEANS `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` OF "Hope Foundation Limited", entries, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`the opinion that the name is unobjectionable` MEANS `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` OF "Hope Foundation Limited", EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the opinion that the name is likely to mislead the public` MEANS `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` OF "Hope Foundation Limited", EMPTY, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`the opinion that the name gives the impression of a connection that does not exist` MEANS `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` OF "Hope Foundation Limited", EMPTY, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`the opinion that the name is offensive` MEANS `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` OF "Hope Foundation Limited", EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE


§§ `More applications, and the charity and the previous names`

-- Lodged on 1 March 2026, complete on 20 March 2026, with a payment to a governor on 10 March 2026 that the application does not disclose.
`the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and complete on 20 March 2026, with an undisclosed payment on 10 March 2026` MEANS `Application for registration` WITH
    dates IS `dates: lodged on 1 March 2026, complete on 20 March 2026`
    `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `particulars: everything provided, paragraph (iii) does not apply`
    `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `documents: all provided`
    `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `financial details: a payment on 10 March 2026 made and not disclosed`
    `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `other requirements: none arise`
    `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS EMPTY

`the application lodged on 1 March 2026 and not yet complete` MEANS `the base application with dates` `dates: lodged on 1 March 2026, not yet complete`

`the use of a previous registered name that is not related to a registered name` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Hope Foundation"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS LIST "Hope Foundation"
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS FALSE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

`the use of a previous registered name that is related and not undesirable in its context` MEANS `Name used by a registered charity` WITH
    `name used` IS "Hope Foundation"
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS LIST "Hope Foundation"
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS TRUE
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS FALSE

`the charity registered as Hope Foundation Limited` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS `a Jersey company that is a registered charity`
    `registration number` IS "JC-2026-001"
    `registered name` IS "Hope Foundation Limited"
    `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
    `date registered` IS YMD 2026 4 2
    `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
    `registered charitable purposes` IS EMPTY
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "Relief of poverty in Jersey"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE


-- A charity that has been deregistered: its entity stands in the historic section (Article 1: it is no longer a registered charity).
`a Jersey company that was registered and has been deregistered` MEANS Entity WITH
    name IS "Hope Foundation Limited"
    `standing on the register` IS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
    `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
    `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
    governors IS LIST `governor Anna`
    purposes IS EMPTY

`the register entry of the charity that has been deregistered` MEANS `Registered charity` WITH
    entity IS `a Jersey company that was registered and has been deregistered`
    `registration number` IS "JC-2019-007"
    `registered name` IS "Hope Foundation Limited"
    `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
    `date registered` IS YMD 2019 5 1
    `date deregistered` IS JUST (YMD 2026 1 15)
    `registered charitable purposes` IS EMPTY
    `registered public benefit statement` IS "Relief of poverty in Jersey"
    `is an organized religious charity` IS FALSE

§§ `Cases used by more than one test module`

-- The bars on granting an application (Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c)), each on top of the base case.
`the case where a reported fitness issue is undetermined` MEANS `the base case` `but with the Article 19(9)(c) bar as` TRUE
`the case where the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` MEANS `the base case` `but with the court order as` TRUE
`the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the Article 19(9)(c) bar as` TRUE) `but with the court order as` TRUE
`the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the name is undesirable` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the Article 19(9)(c) bar as` TRUE) `but with the name as` TRUE
`the case where a fitness issue is undetermined and the copy of the constitution is missing` MEANS (`the base case` `but with the Article 19(9)(c) bar as` TRUE) `but with the application as` (`the base application with documents` `documents: no copy of the constitution`)

§§ `The case, run through the headline decisions`

GIVEN case IS A `Case under Article 11(4)`
GIVETH A `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration`
`the duty in` case MEANS
    `Art 11 the duty of the Commissioner on the application` (case's reading) (case's application) (case's `an Order under Article 13(9) applies`) (case's `Article 19(5) complied with`) (case's applicant) (case's `meets the charity test`) (case's findings) (case's `principal address in Jersey`) (case's `name undesirable`) (case's `Article 19(9)(c) bar`) (case's `court order not to register`)

GIVEN case IS A `Case under Article 11(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision in` case MEANS
    `Art 11 what the Commissioner must do on the application` (case's reading) (case's application) (case's `an Order under Article 13(9) applies`) (case's `Article 19(5) complied with`) (case's applicant) (case's `meets the charity test`) (case's findings) (case's `principal address in Jersey`) (case's `name undesirable`) (case's `Article 19(9)(c) bar`) (case's `court order not to register`)

GIVEN case IS A `Case under Article 11(4)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
`the duty to register in` case MEANS
    `Art 11(4) the Commissioner must register the applicant` (case's reading) (case's application) (case's `an Order under Article 13(9) applies`) (case's `Article 19(5) complied with`) (case's applicant) (case's `meets the charity test`) (case's findings) (case's `principal address in Jersey`) (case's `name undesirable`) (case's `Article 19(9)(c) bar`) (case's `court order not to register`)

GIVEN case IS A `Case under Article 11(4)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 11`
`the duty to refuse in` case MEANS
    `Art 11(5) the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant` (case's reading) (case's application) (case's `an Order under Article 13(9) applies`) (case's `Article 19(5) complied with`) (case's applicant) (case's `meets the charity test`) (case's findings) (case's `principal address in Jersey`) (case's `name undesirable`) (case's `Article 19(9)(c) bar`) (case's `court order not to register`)

GIVEN case IS A `Case under Article 11(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant complies in` case MEANS
    `Art 11(4) the applicant has complied with Article 11(2), the Regulations and Article 19(5)` (case's reading) (case's application) (case's `an Order under Article 13(9) applies`) (case's `Article 19(5) complied with`)

GIVEN case IS A `Case under Article 11(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the six matters are found in` case MEANS
    `Art 11(4) the six matters are found` (case's reading) (case's application) (case's `an Order under Article 13(9) applies`) (case's `Article 19(5) complied with`) (case's applicant) (case's `meets the charity test`) (case's findings) (case's `principal address in Jersey`) (case's `name undesirable`)

